        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): UTF-8 WebSocket requests survive split writes",
        "body": "<!--\nOptional linked context:\nAdd a visible `Closes #<issue-number>` or `Related: #<issue-number>` line\nbelow this comment.\n\nRequired PR title:\ntype: user-facing description\nUse a parenthesized scope only when it adds clarity:\nfix(auth): login redirect loops when session cookie is expired\n\nTypes: feat, fix, improve, refactor, docs, chore.\nFor fixes, describe the user-visible symptom and trigger:\nfix: task list fails to load when user has no environments\nAvoid implementation details such as:\nfix: add null check to task query\n-->\n\n<details>\n<summary>Additional instructions</summary>\n\n**MUST:** Keep **Allow edits from maintainers** enabled for this PR so maintainers\ncan help update the branch when needed.\n\n</details>\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Codex JSON-RPC requests can be corrupted or sent as partial frames when a UTF-8 character or line boundary is split across Writable chunks.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe WebSocket transport now incrementally decodes UTF-8 bytes and retains an incomplete line until its terminating newline arrives. On stream finish it flushes a complete unterminated final frame.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCodex app-server WebSocket users can send JSON-RPC payloads containing multi-byte characters reliably, independent of Node stream chunk boundaries.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused extension test: 3 tests passed, including a JSON-RPC frame whose emoji bytes are split between writes.\n- `pnpm tsgo:extensions:test` passed.\n- Targeted `oxlint` passed for the transport and test files.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Live localhost Codex app-server proof: started `codex app-server --listen ws://127.0.0.1:<ephemeral>`, sent an `initialize` JSON-RPC request with the emoji's UTF-8 bytes split across WebSocket fragments, and received the matching response:\n\n  ```json\n  {\"endpoint\":\"ws://127.0.0.1:<ephemeral>\",\"split_utf8_fragment\":true,\"response_id\":1,\"server_version\":\"present\"}\n  ```\n\nThe remaining `Critical Quality (network-runtime-boundary)` CI failure reports the unchanged main-baseline file `src/infra/push-apns-http2.ts:124`; the CI gate aggregates that unrelated result.\n",
        "branch": "fix/problem-websocket-utf8-chunk-framing",
